{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"调研 2025 年下半年 CP（Constraint Programming）/ SAT / INFORMS / EURO 等会议新论文中跟我们项目相关的方向。\n\n## 项目背景\n\n终末地工业规划器 70×70 网格 266 设施 exact LBBD 求解器（CP-SAT-based）。168h 长跑探索 ε-Certified 三阶段（25h/50h/85h）。已确定方向：\n- Logic-Based Benders Decomposition (master + binding + routing + flow)\n- ε-Certified anytime convergence\n- Combinatorial Benders Cuts (Codato-Fischetti)\n- ML4CO (GNN + ImLearn + AlphaEvolve cut discovery)\n- 工业 CP-SAT 实践（OnlyEnforceIf 重构、precheck、cut persistence）\n\n## 上次调研\n\nR3 `a4438d81d0b74ba38`（2026-05-08）\"Recent CP/CPAIOR papers 2024-2026\"：调到 Huub solver (Dekker CP'25), LLG (Baauw CP'25), DynamicSAT, ViolationLS。\nR5 `a0a1880745aab67e3`（2026-05-08）\"INFORMS / EURO industrial\"：找到 Solar Plant IJOC 2024。\n\n调研时是 2026-05-08，引用截至 2024 年 + 早期 2025。\n\n## 时间窗口（半年新进展）\n\n- **CP 2025**（7 月）已开过：proceedings 应该已发布\n- **SAT 2025**（8 月）已开过：proceedings + competition 结果\n- **CPAIOR 2025**（5-6 月）已开过：proceedings\n- **INFORMS Annual Meeting 2025**（10 月 Phoenix）已开过\n- **EURO 2025**（6 月，Leeds）已开过\n- **ICAPS 2025** / **AAAI 2025** / **NeurIPS 2025**（12 月）\n\n## 调研任务\n\n**用 WebSearch / WebFetch 查 dblp / Google Scholar / 官方 proceedings**：\n\n1. **CP 2025 proceedings**（drops.dagstuhl.de/lipics/CP2025）：找跟 LBBD / Benders / ε-Certified / industrial CP-SAT / 2D placement 直接相关的 paper（最多 5 篇）\n\n2. **SAT 2025 proceedings**：跟 ε-bound / cut sharing / parallel SAT / IPASIR-UP / VeriPB 相关的 paper（最多 3 篇）\n\n3. **CPAIOR 2025 proceedings**：industrial CP-SAT / Benders 工程 paper（最多 3 篇）\n\n4. **INFORMS Annual 2025**：能找到的 placement / 2D packing / max_lex CP industrial 案例（最多 3 篇）\n\n5. **arXiv 2025 H2 trending**：search \"logic-based benders decomposition\", \"anytime cp\", \"epsilon-certified\", \"cut pool\"（最多 3 篇）\n\n每篇必须有 URL + 一句话 takeaway + 是否影响项目当前方向。\n\n## 输出格式（不超过 700 字，中文）\n\n```\n## CP 2025 (3-5 篇)\n- [Title (CP 2025)](URL): one-liner takeaway. 影响项目: [P1 编号 / 新方向 / 无]\n\n## SAT 2025 (1-3 篇)\n...\n\n## CPAIOR 2025 (1-3 篇)\n...\n\n## INFORMS / EURO 2025 (1-3 篇)\n...\n\n## arXiv H2 (1-3 篇)\n...\n\n## 总结\n- 改变路线图的 paper: [无 / X 篇]\n- 加 watchlist 的 paper: [Y 篇]\n- 直接可落地: [Z 篇]\n```\n\n## 操作准则\n\n- 必须 WebSearch / WebFetch 实际 proceedings / arXiv\n- 不要凭训练数据列假 title\n- 一篇没找到就说\"找不到 / 仅限 abstract\"\n- 简洁，不展开 paper 内容\n\n开始。"},"uuid":"3a6ccbaf-6938-4ed9-b923-b02710ebf4cb","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:36.249Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3a6ccbaf-6938-4ed9-b923-b02710ebf4cb","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_delta","addedNames":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"addedLines":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"removedNames":[],"readdedNames":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"061d92b4-a312-430f-a4fd-3f19b65f2f85","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:36.250Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"061d92b4-a312-430f-a4fd-3f19b65f2f85","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \"rebind ctrl+s\", \"add a chord shortcut\", \"change the submit key\", \"customize keybindings\".\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace. - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep running /babysit-prs\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\n- schedule: Create, update, list, or run scheduled remote agents (routines) that execute on a cron schedule. - When the user wants to schedule a recurring remote agent, set up automated tasks, create a cron job for Claude Code, or manage their scheduled agents/routines. Also use when the user wants a one-time scheduled run (\"run this once at 3pm\", \"remind me to check X tomorrow\").\n- claude-api: Build, debug, and optimize Claude API / Anthropic SDK apps. Apps built with this skill should include prompt caching. Also handles migrating existing Claude API code between Claude model versions (4.5 → 4.6, 4.6 → 4.7, retired-model replacements).\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for the Claude API, Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature (caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku) in a file; questions about prompt caching / cache hit rate in an Anthropic SDK project.\nSKIP: file imports `openai`/other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`/`*-generic.py`, provider-neutral code, general programming/ML.\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\n- review: Review a pull request\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","skillCount":10,"isInitial":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"98b23ab0-138d-4e9a-ab8b-b44ecd56a455","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:36.251Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
