{"parentUuid":"fc640ba2-e55d-4ba0-9ccf-51223cc073cd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01T13H3ifmJKPXPsoWQzh5hE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012EtYvRJ8SwLgthRzvzASp8","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"arXiv 2025 \"logic-based Benders decomposition\" anytime epsilon certified"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16250,"cache_read_input_tokens":11009,"output_tokens":344,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16250},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":11009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16250,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CassYnFTeZv2YsYce4Joh","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2601707a-dc4f-41b5-8139-2a4aeab22a40","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:47.225Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d0dc58e3-e89a-4bdf-98de-284a7015c031","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NpWWG9VsFc7ynZrs6mKoRs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP 2025 proceedings dagstuhl LIPIcs Constraint Programming logic-based Benders decomposition\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of ...\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.0/LIPIcs.CP.2025.0.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solving logic-based benders decomposition master problems with constraint programming and domain-independent dynamic programming | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-025-09382-1\"},{\"title\":\"Anytime and Exact Search for Planning Problems: How to explore a DP-based state transition graph with A*, CP and LS? (Invited Talk)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.2\"},{\"title\":\"Solving LBBD Master Problems with Constraint Programming and Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2024.32\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint-Based In-Station Train Dispatching - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.33\"},{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint programming and logic-based Benders decomposition for the integrated process planning and scheduling problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305048322002298\"},{\"title\":\"Planning and Scheduling by Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.1060.0371\"},{\"title\":\"Modeling and Solving a Composite Structure Design Problem with Constraint Programming (Short Paper)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.41\"}]\n\nI've found relevant information about the CP 2025 proceedings. Here are the key results:\n\n## CP 2025 Conference Proceedings\n\nThe 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025) proceedings are published in Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), Volume 340, by Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik (2025).\n\nThe conference was held in Glasgow, Scotland from August 10-15, 2025 and is co-located with the 28th International Conference on Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing (SAT 2025), the 18th International Symposium on Combinatorial Search (SoCS 2025), and the 23rd International Workshop on Satisfiability Modulo Theories (SMT 2025).\n\n## Logic-based Benders Decomposition Research\n\nResearch investigating Constraint Programming (CP) and Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming (DIDP) to solve the master problem in Logic-based Benders Decomposition (LBBD) models focuses on the challenge of feasibility cut formulation. Experimental results show that CP and DIDP approaches outperform a mixed-integer programming (MIP) based master problem and the state-of-the-art monolithic MIP model.\n\nThe proceedings contain papers on various constraint programming topics, including applications to scheduling, planning, and optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fbb74de9-1735-4555-8dd0-b2a878c5fb04","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:50.655Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d0dc58e3-e89a-4bdf-98de-284a7015c031","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3dc28469-94bc-4d34-8730-7c15c13a54e3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KjZn9Q3YcmCZN45ru6rcpa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT 2025 proceedings conference satisfiability cut sharing IPASIR-UP VeriPB\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"The International Conferences on Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing (SAT)\",\"url\":\"https://satisfiability.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG (Short Paper)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42\"},{\"title\":\"Proceedings & Accepted Papers - SAT 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satisfiability.org/SAT25/papers/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT: Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=2551\"},{\"title\":\"RustSAT: A Library for SAT Solving in Rust Christoph Jabs # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol341-sat2025/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.15/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.15.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"ipasir/sat at master · biotomas/ipasir\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/biotomas/ipasir/tree/master/sat\"},{\"title\":\"rustsat - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/rustsat/latest/rustsat/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2023\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/\"}]\n\nI found information related to your search query. Here's what I discovered:\n\nSAT 2025 is the 28th International Conference on Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing, held in Glasgow, UK (2025).\n\nThe SAT 2025 proceedings are published as volume 341 of LIPIcs and available at the Dagstuhl website.\n\nRegarding the specific technologies mentioned in your query:\n\n- **IPASIR-UP**: IPASIR-UP is a user propagators interface for CDCL, presented at SAT 2023 in LIPIcs volume 271. It enables certifying and verifying use cases, with proof systems like VeriPB potentially verifying clause deletion steps.\n\n- **VeriPB**: VeriPB is used as part of an efficient toolchain for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization, implementing proof logging for techniques including cut generation.\n\nThe search results show various SAT 2025 papers including topics related to SAT solving, constraint programming, and proof verification, though I did not find a specific paper explicitly focused on \"cut sharing\" in the SAT 2025 proceedings in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"96443806-e7f3-4e9f-9658-008b22108374","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:52.906Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3dc28469-94bc-4d34-8730-7c15c13a54e3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fc640ba2-e55d-4ba0-9ccf-51223cc073cd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0173Rcnxwb7hRjr3GTGg2TKQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPAIOR 2025 proceedings industrial CP-SAT applications\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPAIOR Conference Series\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR: Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=574\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/cfp/cpaior-2025-integration-of-ai-and-or-techniques-in-constraint-programming_227\"},{\"title\":\"[CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/isaim/c/-zsNiQty_N8\"},{\"title\":\"Disjunctive Scheduling in Tempo - DROPS - Schloss Dagstuhl\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.13\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025: International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.myhuiban.com/conference/2409\"},{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/conference/cpaior\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CPAIOR 2025 proceedings and industrial CP-SAT applications:\n\n## CPAIOR 2025 Conference Details\n\nThe 22nd International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research will be held in Melbourne, Australia from November 10 to November 13, 2025.\n\n## Proceedings Publication\n\nThe conference proceedings will be published in the Springer Lecture Notes in Computer Science series. CPAIOR 2025 will include 32 Papers in 2 Volumes.\n\n## Focus on Industrial Applications\n\nThe conference strongly encourages regular papers or experience reports showcasing CP/AI/OR techniques on challenging real-world applications. High-quality papers from a single area, as well as applications showcasing CP/AI/OR on challenging practical problems, are also a focus of the conference series.\n\nWhile the search results indicate that CPAIOR 2025 welcomes papers on industrial applications and advanced solver techniques like CP-SAT, the specific proceedings with papers on CP-SAT industrial applications have not yet been published, as the conference is scheduled for November 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7484636b-771a-4440-8b24-4061d53474b1","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:53.071Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fc640ba2-e55d-4ba0-9ccf-51223cc073cd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2601707a-dc4f-41b5-8139-2a4aeab22a40","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012EtYvRJ8SwLgthRzvzASp8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"arXiv 2025 \"logic-based Benders decomposition\" anytime epsilon certified\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Enhanced logic-based Benders decomposition methods for the distributed heterogeneous non-permutation flow shop scheduling problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 63 , No 24 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2025.2553820?mi=ik0enr\"},{\"title\":\"[1910.11944] Logic-based Benders decomposition for large-scale optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.11944\"},{\"title\":\"Nested logic-based Benders decomposition for disaster preparedness planning with horizontal coordination: IISE Transactions: Vol 58 , No 4 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/24725854.2025.2491495\"},{\"title\":\"Combining Optimisation and Simulation Using Logic Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.08390\"},{\"title\":\"[2305.11969] Logic-Based Benders Decomposition in Answer Set Programming for Chronic Outpatients Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.11969\"},{\"title\":\"An Enhanced Logic-Based Bender’s Decomposition Algorithm with Proximity Principle for Simulator-Based Distillation Process Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-9717/13/4/977\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-based-benders-decomposition-lbbd-4e47b3ae-690a-44a4-9d80-a191b385b4e6\"},{\"title\":\"[2209.02936] A Double-oracle, Logic-based Benders decomposition approach to solve the K-adaptability problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.02936\"},{\"title\":\"Combining optimisation and simulation using logic-based Benders decomposition - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S037722172300591X\"},{\"title\":\"Enhanced Logic-Based Benders Decomposition Approaches for Flexible Job Shop Scheduling Benchmark Problem with Discrete Operation Sequence Flexibility - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S100093452600074X\"}]\n\nI searched for papers on arXiv from 2025 related to logic-based Benders decomposition with \"anytime epsilon certified\" in the query. The search results returned several recent papers on logic-based Benders decomposition, though none of the results directly matched all the specific terms you're looking for.\n\nThe search results include:\n\n1. **Recent 2025 Papers on LBBD**: Several papers from 2025 applying logic-based Benders decomposition to various problems, including the Distributed Heterogeneous Non-Permutation Flowshop Scheduling Problem, where jobs are assigned to factories and job sequences can vary across machines.\n\n2. **General LBBD Overview**: Logic-based Benders decomposition (LBBD) is a substantial generalization of classical Benders decomposition that allows the subproblem to be any optimization problem rather than specifically a linear or nonlinear programming problem.\n\n3. **Application Domains**: The results show LBBD being applied to scheduling, stochastic programming, and optimization problems, but I didn't find a specific arXiv paper from 2025 that combines all your search terms (anytime, epsilon, certified).\n\nIf you're looking for a specific paper with these exact terms, it's possible the paper may be very recent or uses different terminology. Would you like me to search with different keywords, or do you have additional information about the paper you're looking for?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5c757da6-a870-4bed-b3c3-3e4e12752004","timestamp":"2026