{"parentUuid":"d419a5cd-5ef7-4139-8e8a-2bba3a857502","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Krff1SBFn7j7waaTAr1pGK","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the provided content, here are papers related to your specified topics:\n\n**Certified Reasoning:**\n- \"Certifying Projected Knowledge Compilation\" by Randal Bryant, Yong Kiam Tan, Marijn Heule\n  https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.8\n\n- \"Efficient Certified Reasoning for Binarized Neural Networks\" by Jiong Yang et al.\n  https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.32\n\n**Optimization:**\n- \"An Algebraic Approach to MaxCSP\" by Ilario Bonacina, Jordi Levy\n  https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.6\n\n- \"Analyzing Reformulation Performance in Core-Guided MaxSAT Solving\" by Andre Schidler, Stefan Szeider\n  https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.26\n\n- \"Core-Guided Linear Programming-based Maximum Satisfiability\" by George Katsirelos\n  https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.17\n\n**Distributed/Parallel:**\n- \"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design\" by Dominik Schreiber et al.\n  https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27\n\n**Note:** The provided webpage does not list papers specifically addressing parallel SAT with clause sharing, IPASIR-UP, VeriPB proofs, or cube-and-conquer strategies."}]},"uuid":"8c437aa6-5e49-4bf2-bea1-ba4051545164","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:07.961Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d419a5cd-5ef7-4139-8e8a-2bba3a857502","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"898bb4f6-2655-4cc7-a278-73d7caf36bf6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HQxDy3aMn2cMzc4NCWuDYU","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP 2025 Papers Matching Your Criteria\n\nBased on the provided conference proceedings, here are the relevant papers:\n\n## Anytime Search\n**\"Anytime and Exact Search for Planning Problems: How to explore a DP-based state transition graph with A*, CP and LS?\"**\n- Author: Christine Solnon\n- URL: https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.2\n- Focus: \"Anytime search, Time Dependent TSP-TW\"\n\n## Large Neighborhood Search\n**\"Dependency-Curated Large Neighbourhood Search\"**\n- Authors: Frej Knutar Lewander, Pierre Flener, Justin Pearson\n- URL: https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.20\n- Focus: \"Large Neighbourhood Search (LNS), Constraint-Based Local Search (CBLS)\"\n\n## Industrial CP Applications\n**\"Solving the Agile Earth Observation Satellite Scheduling Problem with CP and Local Search\"**\n- Authors: Valentin Antuori, Damien T. Wojtowicz, Emmanuel Hebrard\n- URL: https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.3\n- Focus: \"Local Search, Greedy Algorithms, Aerospace Applications\"\n\n**\"Modeling and Explaining an Industrial Workforce Allocation and Scheduling Problem\"**\n- Authors: Ignace Bleukx, Ryma Boumazouza, Tias Guns, Nadine Laage, Guillaume Poveda\n- URL: https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.6\n\n## 2D Packing/Placement\n**\"Optimizing 2D Cutting: A Bin Packing Approach to Minimize Scraps and Maximize Their Reusability\"**\n- Authors: Manuel Chastenay, Xavier Zwingmann, Claude-Guy Quimper, Jonathan Gaudreault\n- URL: https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.7\n\n**Note:** Papers specifically addressing Benders decomposition, LBBD, epsilon-optimal solutions, or parallel CP were not identified in the provided excerpt."}]},"uuid":"8543817e-2bd6-4298-a64a-67ae5a640e92","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:08.267Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"898bb4f6-2655-4cc7-a278-73d7caf36bf6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a3892e3e-9e31-4f79-98c2-adfbc7a5ac61","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F8oDoSARTNjQ8SmgGLeWhg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPAIOR 2025 Springer LNCS proceedings papers Melbourne\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research: 22nd International Conference, CPAIOR 2025, Melbourne, VIC, Australia, November 10–13, 2025, Proceedings, Part II | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-95976-9\"},{\"title\":\"‎Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research by Guido Tack on Apple Books\",\"url\":\"https://books.apple.com/au/book/integration-of-constraint-programming-artificial/id6747924321\"},{\"title\":\"Theory Announcements: [DMANET] [CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://dmatheorynet.blogspot.com/2024/09/dmanet-cpaior-2025-call-for-papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research By Guido Tack | World of Books US\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldofbooks.com/products/integration-of-constraint-programming-artificial-intelligence-and-operations-res-book-guido-tack-9783031959721\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR Conference Series\",\"url\":\"https://cpaior.org/\"},{\"title\":\"[CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/isaim/c/-zsNiQty_N8\"},{\"title\":\"International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/conference/cpaior\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025\"},{\"title\":\"Proceedings | HCI International 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.hci.international/proceedings.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the CPAIOR 2025 Springer LNCS proceedings:\n\nThe two-volume set LNCS 15762-15763 constitutes the proceedings of the 22nd International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research, CPAIOR 2025, held in Melbourne, VIC, Australia.\n\nThe 30 full papers and the 2 short papers presented in the proceedings were carefully reviewed and selected from a total of 68 submissions. The proceedings are available through Springer, with the eBook ISBN 978-3-031-95976-9 published on 28 June 2025.\n\nThe conference featured a masterclass and several joint invited talks that covered topics of interest at the intersection of constraint programming, artificial Intelligence, operations research, planning and scheduling, and knowledge representation.\n\nYou can access the proceedings directly through the Springer Nature Link at: https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-95976-9\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"29cb90b6-0684-426d-8b2d-50473a06cf54","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:08.899Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a3892e3e-9e31-4f79-98c2-adfbc7a5ac61","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c763c8cc-99f0-4777-8844-72520a1904d2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NDC2EhNy9dGg18iNJi7QzN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"INFORMS Annual Meeting 2025 Phoenix CP-SAT 2D packing placement max-area\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 INFORMS Annual Meeting - INFORMS\",\"url\":\"https://www.informs.org/Meetings-Conferences/INFORMS-Conference-Calendar/2025-INFORMS-Annual-Meeting\"},{\"title\":\"Agenda - 2025 INFORMS Annual Meeting\",\"url\":\"https://meetings.informs.org/wordpress/annual2025/agenda/\"},{\"title\":\"Register - 2025 INFORMS Annual Meeting\",\"url\":\"https://meetings.informs.org/wordpress/annual/register/\"},{\"title\":\"2025 informs annual meeting\",\"url\":\"https://3449182.fs1.hubspotusercontent-na1.net/hubfs/3449182/INFORMS%202025%20Annual%20Meeting_Prospectus.pdf?hsCtaTracking=085efac7-fee0-48ab-95a6-14dcebb8512f%7C0d0c8b5f-1379-4f4f-8b71-11d5b296860f\"},{\"title\":\"[Searchable Schedule At-A-Glance] 2025 INFORMS ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.facebook.com/INFORMSpage/posts/searchable-schedule-at-a-glance-2025-informs-annual-meeting-httpsbitly44xsjxd-oc/1427082082084674/\"},{\"title\":\"INFORMS Conference Calendar - INFORMS\",\"url\":\"https://www.informs.org/Meetings-Conferences/INFORMS-Conference-Calendar\"},{\"title\":\"INFORMS Annual Meeting Programs - INFORMS\",\"url\":\"https://www.informs.org/Meetings-Conferences/Program-Archives/INFORMS-Annual-Meeting-Programs\"},{\"title\":\"INFORMS Annual Meeting (Oct 2025), Atlanta USA - Conference\",\"url\":\"https://10times.com/e1d2-d2x4-6zkf-f\"},{\"title\":\"Meetings & Conferences - INFORMS\",\"url\":\"https://www.informs.org/Meetings-Conferences\"},{\"title\":\"2025 INFORMS Annual Meeting | Atlanta\",\"url\":\"https://meetings.informs.org/wordpress/annual2025/\"}]\n\nThe search results show information about the 2025 INFO