{"parentUuid":"667fd357-e1a4-45bb-8d02-6319ee9e1c3f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NSM8vfoaT8hme76avbajdU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01851S4qE5sFR6DYD2BvvWZv","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"arXiv 2025 \"combinatorial Benders\" cuts learned ML4CO neural cut"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4428,"cache_read_input_tokens":32593,"output_tokens":473,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4428},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":32593,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4428,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CassaqAe3MVGYZhmZqhKf","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"15183e56-0f8e-41fd-ba43-4e3a5e906043","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:16.998Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"15183e56-0f8e-41fd-ba43-4e3a5e906043","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01851S4qE5sFR6DYD2BvvWZv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"arXiv 2025 \"combinatorial Benders\" cuts learned ML4CO neural cut\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Learning to Cut: Reinforcement Learning for Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2605.06516\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal Training via Combinatorial Benders' Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2207.07690\"},{\"title\":\"Graph-Based Imitation and Reinforcement Learning for Eﬀicient\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.11870\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/combinatorial-benders-cuts\"},{\"title\":\"[2406.11897] A Benchmark for Maximum Cut: Towards Standardization of the Evaluation of Learned Heuristics for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.11897\"},{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1838192/FULLTEXT02.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by Strengthening Cuts with Graph Neural Networks | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378249676_Speeding_Up_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition_by_Strengthening_Cuts_with_Graph_Neural_Networks\"},{\"title\":\"Graph-Based Imitation and Reinforcement Learning for Efficient Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.11870v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2203.02433] The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Competition (ML4CO): Results and Insights\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02433\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant papers related to your query about combinatorial Benders cuts, learned cutting planes, and ML4CO (Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization):\n\n## Key Results\n\n**Recent 2025 Paper on Learning to Cut for Benders Decomposition:**\nThe search results include a paper titled \"Learning to Cut: Reinforcement Learning for Benders Decomposition\" from arXiv (2605.06516), which appears to be directly relevant to your query.\n\n**Graph-Based Learning for Benders Decomposition:**\nAnother recent work introduces an end-to-end graph-based agent for accelerating Benders Decomposition, where the agent's policy is parameterized by a graph neural network taking a bipartite graph representation of the master problem, trained using a two-stage approach combining imitation and reinforcement learning.\n\n**Neural Cut Strengthening with GNNs:**\nWork has been done applying graph neural networks in an autoregressive fashion to approximate the compilation of irreducible cuts in logic-based Benders decomposition, tested on job scheduling problems.\n\n**ML4CO Context:**\nThe ML4CO competition aims at improving state-of-the-art combinatorial optimization solvers by replacing key heuristic components, with featured tasks including finding the best feasible solution, producing the tightest optimality certificate, and giving appropriate solver configuration.\n\nThese papers represent the intersection of neural networks, cutting-plane methods, and learned optimization approaches within the ML4CO research area.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"de33d273-f1bb-4f12-95ed-a05675431a12","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:22.995Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"15183e56-0f8e-41fd-ba43-4e3a5e906043","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","