{"parentUuid":"667fd357-e1a4-45bb-8d02-6319ee9e1c3f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tc7XC16cqCZGEfXVadnCtS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"arXiv 2025 \"anytime\" CP-SAT constraint programming industrial placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Enhancing Constraint Programming via Supervised Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2211.14492\"},{\"title\":\"Investigating Constraint Programming and Hybrid Methods for Real World Industrial Test Laboratory Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/1911.04766\"},{\"title\":\"PyJobShop: Solving scheduling problems with constraint programming in Python\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.13483\"},{\"title\":\"CP-Agent: Agentic Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.07468v1\"},{\"title\":\"On Continuous Optimization for Constraint Satisfaction Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.04480v1\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"[2510.05774] ConstraintLLM: A Neuro-Symbolic Framework for Industrial-Level Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.05774\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers - CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/cfp.html\"},{\"title\":\"[2605.04052] Constraint-Aware Execution Planning for Hybrid Space-Ground Compute Workloads\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04052\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant papers from 2025 related to constraint programming and CP-SAT, though the specific combination of \"anytime,\" \"CP-SAT,\" and \"industrial placement\" didn't return a single exact match. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key 2025 Papers on CP-SAT and Constraint Programming:\n\n1. **PyJobShop** PyJobShop conducts a large-scale numerical experiment to compare the performance between OR-Tools and CP Optimizer using more than 9,000 benchmark instances from the machine scheduling and project scheduling literature.\n\n2. **ConstraintLLM** ConstraintLLM is the first LLM specifically designed for CP modeling, and it includes IndusCP, the first industrial-level benchmark for CP modeling, which contains 140 challenging tasks from various domains.\n\n3. **CP-Agent: Agentic Constraint Programming** CPMpy's solver-agnostic design allows modeling problems once and solving them using various backends, including CP, MIP, SMT, and SAT solvers.\n\n4. **Anytime Approaches**: Anytime MaxSAT solvers that compute low-cost solutions within a limited available computational time have significantly improved in recent years.\n\nThe search results show active research in constraint programming for industrial applications in 2025, though I couldn't locate a paper with that exact title combination on arXiv. If you have a more specific paper identifier or author name, I can conduct a more targeted search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"77178de7-d492-42d5-b8cb-279da6538695","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:23.165Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"667fd357-e1a4-45bb-8d02-6319ee9e1c3f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3e4d1038-7daa-4b02-b3bd-d5e866358aa9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VRtKPUR9KQdACj2qpZWmxe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CPAIOR 2025\" Benders decomposition cut accepted paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/cpaior2025/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Theory Announcements: [DMANET] [CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://dmatheorynet.blogspot.com/2024/09/dmanet-cpaior-2025-call-for-papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/cfp/cpaior-2025-integration-of-ai-and-or-techniques-in-constraint-programming_227\"},{\"title\":\"[CPAIOR 2025] — Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/isaim/c/-zsNiQty_N8\"},{\"title\":\"[2605.06516] Learning to Cut: Reinforcement Learning for Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06516\"},{\"title\":\"AI4OPT Researchers Present Optimization Advances and Win Awards at CPAIOR 2025 | Artificial Intelligence Institute for Advances in Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.ai4opt.org/news-events/ai4opt-researchers-present-optimization-advances-and-win-awards-cpaior-2025\"},{\"title\":\"Stronger cuts for Benders’ decomposition for stochastic Unit Commitment Problems based on interval variables – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2025/11/stronger-cuts-for-benders-decomposition-for-stochastic-unit-commitment-problems-based-on-interval-variables/\"},{\"title\":\"Theory Announcements: [DMANET] CPAIOR 2026 – Call for Papers | Rabat, Morocco | May 26–29, 2026\",\"url\":\"http://dmatheorynet.blogspot.com/2025/11/dmanet-cpaior-2026-call-for-papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Literature review on Benders cut selection and a multiple cut generation scheme: INFOR: Information Systems and Operational Research: Vol 64 , No 1 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/03155986.2025.2540205\"},{\"title\":\"A generalized Benders decomposition-based branch and cut ...\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/Papers/Li_Grossmann_GBD_branch_and_cuts.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CPAIOR 2025 and papers related to Benders decomposition cuts:\n\n## CPAIOR 2025 Conference\n\nThe 22nd International Conference on the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research will be held in Melbourne, Australia from November 10 to November 13, 2025.\n\n## Accepted Papers on Benders Decomposition Cuts\n\nThe search results reveal several papers accepted at or presented at CPAIOR 2025 that involve Benders decomposition cuts:\n\n1. **Quantum-Classical Algorithm with Benders Cut Generation**: A novel Benders-cut generation technique was incorporated into a hybrid quantum-classical algorithm, and this work was presented at CPAIOR 2025 by researchers from the NSF AI Institute for Advances in Optimization.\n\n2. **Stronger Cuts for Stochastic Unit Commitment**: A new Benders decomposition approach was proposed that leverages an extended formulation based on interval variables, leading to provably stronger Benders cuts than those derived from the standard 3-bin representation.\n\n3. **Learning-Based Cut Selection**: A framework called Reinforcement Learning for BD (RLBD) was proposed that adaptively selects cuts using a neural network-based stochastic policy trained using a policy gradient method via the REINFORCE algorithm.\n\nThe conference accepts papers on innovative decomposition techniques based on column generation and Benders as a core topic of interest.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b997d281-9d19-4c9d-b2d5-ca20fc08d045","timest