{"parentUuid":"14bc8a17-f184-4d48-b361-590aa4595ca5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KLB4P4bWf5w7HJVhuhUi9e","type":"tool_result","content":"# AI4OPT Research at CPAIOR 2025\n\n## Award-Winning Papers\n\n**Best Paper Award:**\n- \"Multi-task Representation Learning for Mixed Integer Linear Programming\" by Junyang Cai\n\n## All AI4OPT Papers Presented\n\n1. \"Multi-task Representation Learning for Mixed Integer Linear Programming\" – Junyang Cai\n2. \"Leveraging Quantum Computing for Accelerated Classical Algorithms in Power Systems Optimization\" – Rosemary Barrass\n3. \"Self-Supervised Penalty-Based Learning for Robust Constrained Optimization\" – Wyame Benslimane\n\n## Papers Related to Specified Topics\n\n**Benders Cuts:**\n- Barrass's quantum-classical work incorporated \"a novel Benders-cut generation technique\" to enhance solution quality while reducing computational demands.\n\n**Hybrid Quantum-Classical Methods:**\n- Barrass presented QC4UC, a hybrid approach combining quantum annealing with classical optimization for power systems problems.\n\n**Industrial Applications (Power Systems/Scheduling):**\n- Barrass's research addressed the unit commitment problem, which \"grid operators solve daily to meet electricity demand while satisfying operational constraints.\"\n\n*Note: No papers specifically on CP-SAT solver were identified in the provided content.*"}]},"uuid":"7fb06b7a-4ef6-4701-b54d-7b2f6045aa20","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:35.049Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"14bc8a17-f184-4d48-b361-590aa4595ca5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ea4842f7-33ab-463f-9153-f0e37b911029","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M4BwsS6GbgLssH2gzsqGVU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"arXiv 2025 \"cut pool\" OR \"cut persistence\" parallel CP-SAT OR-Tools\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parallelized Conflict Graph Cut Generation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2311.03706\"},{\"title\":\"[2204.00491] FrequencyLowCut Pooling -- Plug & Play against Catastrophic Overfitting\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.00491\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found one relevant paper on arXiv that relates to your query:\n\n**The paper \"Parallelized Conflict Graph Cut Generation\" develops efficient parallel conflict graph management including conflict detection, maximal clique generation, clique extension, and clique merging for mixed-integer programming (MIP) solvers.** The work leverages parallel computing to generate a larger pool of cutting planes than what can be practically achieved in serial, with computational experiments demonstrating that the expanded pool of cuts enabled by parallel computing lead to substantial reductions in total MIP solve time.\n\nHowever, the search results don't appear to contain papers specifically matching all your search criteria (particularly related to OR-Tools and CP-SAT in 2025). The first result (arxiv.org/html/2311.03706) appears to be from June 2025 and deals with parallelized cut generation, which is related to your query, but the second result is about neural network pooling and is not relevant.\n\nIf you'd like more specific results, you might want to search arXiv directly with slightly different terms, or let me know if you'd like me to perform another search with modified keywords.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1a2fd96b-2eb4-4a0c-b8e8-1ce203415624","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:36.400Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea4842f7-33ab-463f-9153-f0e37b911029","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
