{"parentUuid":"8ecbcb21-026c-4295-94fa-64daec7c22d6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Fg4eQLH1hruXrCHsM9FCM9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B2iCxq2nfnDD4L8UNsobzY","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"arXiv 2025 GNN Graph Neural Network Benders decomposition scheduling cut strengthening"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1719,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4685,"cache_read_input_tokens":39375,"output_tokens":370,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4685},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1719,"output_tokens":370,"cache_read_input_tokens":39375,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4685,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CasscvXAEa7hECGwx4SVB","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"82b7f27d-2870-4b59-a7d6-befb1ef8ab72","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:43.526Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8ecbcb21-026c-4295-94fa-64daec7c22d6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0121szmazcZgDNdgdmud9LJt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes\" CP 2025 constraint programming\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes for Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.4\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2025 Accepted Papers\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/accepted_papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting Planes for Constraint ...\",\"url\":\"https://repository.tudelft.nl/file/File_6cb76175-7821-435a-b340-e1621a8450ef\"},{\"title\":\"CP: Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=572\"},{\"title\":\"Cut-based Conﬂict Analysis in Mixed Integer Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2410.15110\"},{\"title\":\"CPAIOR 2025 : Integration of AI and OR Techniques in Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/servlet/event.showcfp?eventid=182533&copyownerid=106070\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Programming and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/CPandOR.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cut-Based Conflict Analysis in Mixed Integer Programming | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2024.0999\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict analysis in CP solving: Explanation generation from constraint decomposition - Archive ouverte HAL\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-03179630\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information about the paper on \"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes for Constraint Programming\" presented at CP 2025.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe paper introduces a novel constraint learning mechanism for Constraint Programming (CP) solvers that integrates cutting planes reasoning into the conflict analysis procedure.\n\n## Key Approach: Lazy Linear Generation (LLG)\n\nThe approach, named Lazy Linear Generation (LLG), can generate linear integer inequalities to prune the search space, rather than propositional clauses as in Lazy Clause Generation (LCG). This combines the strengths of constraint programming (strong propagation through global constraints) with cutting-planes reasoning.\n\n## Technical Details\n\nLinear constraint explanations are presented for various arithmetic constraints and the element constraint. Additionally, when cutting planes reasoning fails to derive a linear constraint, Lazy Clause Generation (LCG) is employed as a fallback mechanism.\n\n## Experimental Results\n\nAn experimental evaluation shows that the improved generality of linear constraints has a practical impact on a CP solver by reducing the number of encountered conflicts in 45% of the benchmark instances.\n\n## Authors and Publication\n\nThe paper \"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes for Constraint Programming\" was presented at the 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025) by Robbin Baauw, Maarten Flippo, and Emir Demirović.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8e3357f6-da9b-4a05-8325-70e84787dbc7","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:49.619Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8ecbcb21-026c-4295-94fa-64daec7c22d6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"82b7f27d-2870-4b59-a7d6-befb1ef8ab72","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B2iCxq2nfnDD4L8UNsobzY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"arXiv 2025 GNN Graph Neural Network Benders decomposition scheduling cut strengthening\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by Strengthening Cuts with Graph Neural Networks | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-53969-5_3\"},{\"title\":\"Speeding up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ac.tuwien.ac.at/files/pub/varga_23b.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by Strengthening Cuts with Graph Neural Networks | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378249676_Speeding_Up_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition_by_Strengthening_Cuts_with_Graph_Neural_Networks\"},{\"title\":\"[2511.11870] Graph-Based Imitation and Reinforcement Learning for Efficient Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.11870\"},{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1838192/FULLTEXT02.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Graph-Based Imitation and Reinforcement Learning for Efficient Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.11870v1\"},{\"title\":\"Graph-Based Imitation and Reinforcement Learning for Eﬀicient\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.11870\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Cut: Reinforcement Learning for Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2605.06516\"},{\"title\":\"Benders Decomposition using Graph Modeling and Multi-Parametric Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.01100\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Optimization with Automated Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.02872v1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant papers on using Graph Neural Networks with Benders decomposition for cut strengthening and scheduling:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n### 1. **\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by Strengthening Cuts with Graph Neural Networks\"**\n\nLogic-based Benders decomposition is a technique to solve optimization problems to optimality by splitting the problem into a master problem and a subproblem, which is used to iteratively produce cuts for the master problem. The work applies a graph neural network in an autoregressive fashion to approximate the compilation of an irreducible cut, which then only requires few postprocessing steps to ensure its validity. \n\nThe approach is tested on a job scheduling problem with a single machine and multiple time windows per job, with results showing that the approach is capable of considerably reducing the number of subproblems that need to be solved and hence the total computational effort.\n\n### 2. **\"Graph-Based Imitation and Reinforcement Learning for Efficient Benders Decomposition\"** (arXiv 2511.11870)\n\nA more recent paper (November 2025) presents an end-to-end graph-based agent for accelerating the computational efficiency of Benders Decomposition, where the agent's policy is parameterized by a graph neural network which takes as input a bipartite graph representation of the master problem and proposes a candidate solution. The agent is trained using a two-stage approach that combines imitation learning and reinforcement learning, with IL used to mimic a solver and obtain a warm-start policy which is then finetuned using RL.\n\nThese papers demonstrate the intersection of GNNs, Benders decomposition, and scheduling optimization that your search query was targeting.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d47a6312-4e9a-4653-bb69-283403337a3c","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:50.601Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"82b7f27d-2870-4b59-a7d6-befb1ef8ab72","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"86dbf41b-e853-4c73-9d8b-87b23c187080","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"ab0787721db5ca990","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XE1XRjDyR6CjGT1hCPE14D","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP 2025 Accepted Papers - Full List with Highlights\n\n## All Accepted Papers (45 total)\n\n1. Transformer-based Feature Learning for Algorithm Selection in Combinatorial Optimisation\n2. Constraint-based In-Station Train Dispatching\n3. Greed is slow on sparse graphs of oriented valued constraints\n4. Analyzing Self-stabilization of Synchronous Unison via Propositional Satisfiability\n5. Learning to Bound for Maximum Common Subgraph Algorithms\n6. Transition Dominance in Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming\n7. Guess and Prove: A Hybrid Approach to Linear Polynomial Recovery in Circuit Verification\n8. Exact Methods for the Travelling Salesperson Problem with Self-Deleting Graphs\n9. Reducing Quantum Circuit Synthesis to #SAT\n10. Aircraft Resource-Constrained Assembly Line Balancing with Learning Effect: a Constraint Programming Approach\n11. Disjunctive Scheduling in Tempo\n12. Balancing Latin Rectangles with LLM-generated Streamliners\n13. Dependency-Curated Large Neighbourhood Search\n14. An Efficient and Uniform CSP Solution Generator Generator\n15. Symmetric Core Learning for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization by Implicit Hitting Sets\n16. Modeling and Explaining an Industrial Workforce Allocation and Scheduling Problem\n17. PrintTalk: A Language for Constraint-based 3D Modelling\n18. Unit Types for MiniZinc\n19. Unite and Lead: Finding Disjunctive Cliques for Scheduling Problems\n20. Optimizing 2D Cutting: A Bin Packing Approach to Minimize Scraps and Maximize their Reusability\n21. Breaking Symmetries with Involutions\n22. An Expansion-Based Approach for Quantified Integer Programming\n23. The Work Task Variation Problem\n24. Scalable Counting of Minimal Trap Spaces and Fixed Points in Boolean Networks\n25. Constraint Models for Klondike\n26. Multi-League Sports Scheduling with Team Interdependencies: An Optimization Model\n27. SLS-Enhanced Core-Boosted Linear Search for Anytime Maximum Satisfiability\n28. Parallel MIP Solving with Dynamic Task Decomposition\n29. Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes for Constraint Programming\n30. RPID: Rust Programmable Interface for Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming\n31. The 3-Decomposition Conjecture: A SAT-Based Approach with Specialized Propagators\n32. Understanding the Impact of Value Selection Heuristics in Scheduling Problems\n33. Solving the Agile Earth Observation Satellite Scheduling Problem with CP and Local Search\n34. Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\n35. BFS-Based Canonical Codes for Generating Graphs with Constraint Programming\n36. From Prediction to Action: A Constraint-Based Approach to Predictive Policing\n37. Cargo Routing Optimization in Liner Shipping Networks\n38. DynamicSAT: Dynamic Configuration Tuning for SAT Solving\n39. Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG\n40. Scheduling Telescope Observations for the European Southern Observatory\n41. Modeling and Solving a Composite Structure Design Problem with Constraint Programming\n\n## Highlighted Papers by Topic\n\n**2D Packing/Placement:**\n- \"Optimizing 2D Cutting: A Bin Packing Approach to Minimize Scraps and Maximize their Reusability\"\n\n**Large Neighborhood Search:**\n- \"Dependency-Curated Large Neighbourhood Search\"\n\n**Cutting Planes/Conflict Analysis:**\n- \"Conflict Analysis Based on Cutting-Planes for Constraint Programming\"\n\n**Anytime Algorithms:**\n- \"SLS-Enhanced Core-Boosted Linear Search for Anytime Maximum Satisfiability\"\n\n**Parallel/Portfolio Methods:**\n- \"Parallel MIP Solving with Dynamic Task Decomposition\"\n\n**ML-Augmented Search:**\n- \"Transformer-based Feature Learning for Algorithm Selection in Combinatorial Optimisation\"\n- \"Balancing Latin Rectangles with LLM-generated Streamliners\"\n\n**Industrial Applications:**\n- \"Constraint-based In-Station Train Dispatching\"\n- \"Aircraft Resource-Constrained Assembly Line Balancing with Learning Effect\"\n- \"Modeling and Explaining an Industrial Workforce Allocation and Scheduling Problem\""}]},"uuid":"a8e2136b-655e-4486-a672-436fcfeeb180","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:54.253Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"86dbf41b-e853-4c73-9d8b-87b23c187080","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
